  "tree": {
    "id": "root",
    "approach": "ANSWERED. Work in the periodic Maya-diagram (bead) model. A semistandard cylindric skew tableau is a chain of n-periodic bead configurations; its weight is the increment sequence of the single scalar u^t = sum_{i=1..m} x^t_i. The M-convex exchange axiom is then realised by sliding ONE bead of ONE row of the chain one site to the left. Main theorem is strictly stronger than WZZ Cor 4.9: supp(s^c_{lambda/mu}(x_1..x_l)) = {alpha : sort(alpha) <| lambdahat} = P_lambdahat cap Z^l, with lambdahat computed by an explicit greedy chain.",
    "trust": "proved",
