        "approach": "UNTUNED POSITIVE CONTROL, run before the instrument was aimed anywhere. WZZ Example 4.2: for w = s_2 s_1 s_0 s_2 in S~_3, F~_w = m_1111 + m_211 + m_22 = s_22 - s_1111. A search over C^{3,m} with d=4 finds exactly one realisation (m=1, mu=(0), lambda=(4)) and the bead model reproduces the published value EXACTLY, negative Schur coefficient included. Separately the ANCHOR: at n=20 the model agrees in all 13 coefficients with an independently coded ordinary skew Kostka computation. Anchor pins the object; the signed separator proves it is not ordinary skew Schur in disguise. SECOND CONTROL (WZZ Figure 5.1, n=5 m=2 weight (1,2,1,2)): compiled their ytableau source to a picture, read the boxes off it, converted via x_i = R_i + i to mu=(0,2), lam=(3,5) in C^{5,2}; their printed tableau is the chain (0,2)<=(0,3)<=(1,4)<=(2,4)<=(3,5), every step certified a cylindric horizontal strip of sizes 1,2,1,2 exactly as printed. This is what fixed the orientation of the dictionary.",
